[sliver] The 1 mm tip land follows the 1.5 mm entry chamfer on the 2.5 mm upper spring leaf. It starts the leaf into the compressor's gap; the full leaf section remains behind the lead-in. Printed on the X end, every layer carries this same supported profile.
click: x=0.000 y=-24.500 z=-22.000

[sliver] The 1 mm tip land follows the 1.5 mm entry chamfer on the 2.5 mm lower spring leaf. It starts the leaf into the compressor's gap; the full leaf section remains behind the lead-in. Printed on the X end, every layer carries this same supported profile.
click: x=0.000 y=-35.500 z=-22.000

[ceiling] The linter is wrong for this part's pose. The clamp prints on its side, on its 18 mm swept profile face, with every layer the same silhouette and nothing needing support (fuse-clamp/README.md, Frame and print; trial-preparation pieces.json `small-petg`). These are Z-facing faces of the profile, vertical in the print. The lint reads ceilings only for a piece bedded on its Z- or Z+ face.
alternatives: Printing on the seating plane would make them real ceilings over the leaves' gap. The lint could read ceilings in a declared turned pose, as it reads ledges.
