[thin] Specific compliant element: the two 2.5 mm leaves are 22 mm cantilevers. They are the one compliant thing in the part, and they take up the compressor gap's tolerance by bending. Each tip is chamfered so it starts into the gap rather than butting its mouth, and the chamfer reads 1.786 mm (fuse-clamp/README.md).
alternatives: Thicker leaves stiffen the press until the gap's tolerance crushes the cutoff or the leaves will not enter. A square tip butts the gap's mouth.
